<title>USA: American Radio sells $200 mln in preferred.</title>
<headline>American Radio sells $200 mln in preferred.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-01-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>The following 144a offering of $200 million in exchangeable preferred stock from American Radio Systems Corp was priced on Monday via Credit Suisse First Boston, according to market sources.</p>
<p>BORROWER AMERICAN RADIO SYSTEMS CORP</p>
<p>AMT $200 MLN	  COUPON 11 3/8 PCT MATURITY 1/15/09</p>
<p>TYPE CUM EXCH PFD   ISS PRICE 100     FIRST PAY DATE 4/15/97</p>
<p>LAST MOODY'S NR     YIELD 11 3/8 PCT  PAY FREQ QUARTERLY</p>
<p>LAST S&amp;P B-MINUS    SPREAD N/A	  CALLABLE NON-CALLABLE</p>
<p>							     FOR FIVE</p>
<p>							     YEARS</p>
<p>NOTE: -Securities Pay-In-Kind (PIK) for first five years.</p>
<p>-Exchangeable for high-yield bonds at discretion of</p>
<p>	    issuer</p>
<p>-Three-year equity call for 35 percent of issue at</p>
<p>	    111.375</p>
<p>-Deal was increased to $200 million from an original</p>
<p>	    amount of $150 million.</p>
<p>((U.S. corporate bond unit, 212 859-1662))</p>
</text>
